      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I encountered the exact same issue.\n\nWhen I created a Group instance, a security gate didn't work.\n\nI investigated and found in the reference that the \"IsInstanceOwner\" property always returns false for Group instances.\n\nI don't think that's a bad behavior, but it would be nice if there was some way to get the Group name when we create a Group instance.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-07-13T14:41:24.382Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently if a world instance is created, you can check the name of the instance creator. It would be very useful to be able to access the name of the group that created the session if it's a group session rather than a normal user session.\n\nUse-case: I'm trying to add functionality for certain groups to be able to tailor the instance of a world to their group using in-world functionality, but without the ability to check the name of the group that created the session, this can't be locked down to only allow the group hosting the session to action it.",
